        "header": "1Introduction",
        "images": [
            {
                "img": "https://arxiv.org/html/2608.12149/2608.12149v1/figures/overview/gated_delta_net_morphology_overview.png",
                "caption": "Figure 1:MA morphology across hybrid configurations in Gated DeltaNet HLA models.MAs formpre-attention spikes(PAS) immediately before full attention layers.\nAs full attention becomes denser, MAs increasingly persist between successive PAS, forminginter-spike plateaus(ISP) and ultimately converging to the stable morphology characteristic of full attention LLMs.\nThe models are from the M-A-P Hybrid Linear Attention Research suite(42).",
                "position": 450
            }
        ]
