    {
        "header": "4A Systematic-Outlier Account of PAS and ISP",
        "images": [
            {
                "img": "https://arxiv.org/html/2608.12149/2608.12149v1/figures/mechanism/pas_lifecycle.png",
                "caption": "Figure 6:Localized write–sink–cancel lifecycle underlying PAS.A representative 1.3B GDN model with a12:112{:}1hybridization ratio is shown.\nA large outlier is written immediately before full attention and subsequently reduced by an opposite-signed update.\nDetailed fixed-coordinate evidence is provided in AppendixE.1.",
                "position": 1035
            },
            {
                "img": "https://arxiv.org/html/2608.12149/2608.12149v1/figures/mechanism/isp_lifecycle.png",
                "caption": "Figure 7:ISP as a delayed-cancellation regime of the systematic-outlier lifecycle.A large outlier written immediately before full attention remains prominent across the intervening linear attention layers and is followed by an opposite-signed update as the plateau dissipates.",
                "position": 1101
            }
        ]
    },
